      {
        "id": "p41-q52-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $k\\dfrac{{}^{n}C_k}{{}^{n}C_{k-1}}=n-k+1$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k\\dfrac{{}^{n}C_k}{{}^{n}C_{k-1}}=n-k+1$.\n\nExpand both combinations into factorials and cancel.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}k\\frac{{}^{n}C_k}{{}^{n}C_{k-1}}&=k\\times\\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\\times\\frac{(k-1)!(n-k+1)!}{n!}\\\\k\\frac{{}^{n}C_k}{{}^{n}C_{k-1}}&=\\frac{k(k-1)!}{k!}\\times\\frac{(n-k+1)!}{(n-k)!}\\\\k\\frac{{}^{n}C_k}{{}^{n}C_{k-1}}&=n-k+1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p41-q52-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p41-q52-b-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Hence, show that",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p41-q52-b-equation",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "center",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\frac{{}^{n}C_1}{{}^{n}C_0}+2\\frac{{}^{n}C_2}{{}^{n}C_1}+3\\frac{{}^{n}C_3}{{}^{n}C_2}+\\cdots+n\\frac{{}^{n}C_n}{{}^{n}C_{n-1}}=\\frac n2(n+1).",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p41-q52-hint",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Hint: Use the result that ",
                  "marks": [
                    "italic"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "1+2+3+\\cdots+n=\\frac n2(n+1)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac n2(n+1)$.\n\nBy part (a), the terms are $n,n-1,\\ldots,1$; use the supplied sum formula.",
          "worked": "Let $S$ denote the left-hand side. By part (a), its $k$th term is $n-k+1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=n+(n-1)+(n-2)+\\cdots+1\\\\S&=1+2+3+\\cdots+n\\\\S&=\\frac n2(n+1).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
  },
